collector
---------

collector is a browser-based evidence collection tool for web applications.

Its purpose is to observe web applications through a real browser, collect
structured observations, and preserve selected artifacts for downstream
analysis.

collector intentionally separates collection from analysis.  It does not attempt
to identify technologies, infer business logic, detect vulnerabilities, or
generate reports.  It records what it observes and leaves interpretation to
other tools.

A collection run navigates to configured targets, discovers additional navigable
pages, records page observations, and preserves selected browser-observed
resources.

The current collector produces:

    - manifest.json
        Run metadata and configured targets.

    - observations.jsonl
        One record for each processed page, including its URL, title and HTML.

    - artifacts.jsonl
        A record for each observed script or stylesheet response whose body is
        preserved, including its URL, SHA-256 hash and stored path.

    - responses.jsonl
        One record for each browser response, including its resource type, URL
        and response headers.

    - artifacts/
        The preserved script and stylesheet bytes.

Artifact files are content-addressed using SHA-256.  Identical bytes encountered
multiple times during a run are stored only once, while artifacts.jsonl
preserves every observation of those bytes.

Page traversal uses an explicit work queue.  Discovered URLs are canonicalized
before being queued, and configured scope rules are applied before pages are
processed.

Configuration is supplied through a versioned JSON configuration file:

    collector --config <file>

An optional output directory can be supplied:

    collector --config <file> --output <directory>

The configuration can also specify HTTP headers that are added to requests made
by the browser:

    {
        "version": 1,
        "targets": [
            "https://example.com",
            "https://foo.example.com"
        ],
        "scope": {
            "include": [
                "example.com",
                "*.example.com"
            ],
            "exclude": [
                "bar.example.com",
                "baz.example.com"
            ]
        },
        "headers": {
            "X-Collector": "collector"
        }
    }

collector is built from small, focused modules with explicit data flow and
structured output.  The implementation favors simple control flow, observable
state and independently testable components.

See docs/ for the project's design philosophy and architectural decisions.
